HEALTH WARNING: don't just run these, they were a proof-of-concept

EXAMPLE: nomadnetwork://cdfa7292616244aff682bdcc073ef161:/page/camera.mu       (manual reload only)

TO WATCH THIS CAMERA: python3 watch_stream.py dcd22b490132414be19f3d08b5d13560   (the command must say the hash of a broadcasting webcam)

DEPENDENCIES (as far as I remember):-

reticulum
nomadnet*
python3
hasciicam - https://github.com/dyne/HasciiCam

The clients don't need hasciicam, just a working reticulum instance and a viewer script

rBrowser can't auto-reload pages so this script shows the output of hasciicam inside the user's terminal
Nomadnet I think wasn't needed. It wants a full terminal environment and negotiates for one with the client, which can't be done rapidly enough so it hangs
Because Reticulum limits packets to 500 bytes even Hasciicam frames need to be sent as chunks. My hasciicam command is hasciicam -m text -s 640x480 -r 0.5 -b 100 -c 100 -g 100 -I -o /tmp/livecam.txt & which is basically 640x480 and 2 frames / second. This is very minimal but in videoconferencing enough to show there is another human there without them being identifiable
Reticulum's actual messaging assumes a sender-and-receiver with encryption keys, so the only way I could find was LXFM Broadcasts


